%chk=probe_fe_porphine_singlet.chk
%mem=16GB
%nprocshared=8
#P HF/6-31G NoSymm Int=NoBasisTransform SCF=(Conver=10,MaxCycle=256)
# Output=(MatrixElement,MO2ElectronIntegrals) Tran=(Full,Force) Window=(83,103)

probe_fe_porphine_singlet: Fe(II) porphine, 37 atoms, ~255 basis functions, closed-shell singlet. Window (83,103) is CAS(22,21) -- 186 electrons gives 93 occupied orbitals, so this is 11 occupied plus 10 virtual, the same active space as the legacy dumps. IMPORTANT: this is a MODEL geometry (idealised D4h, Fe-N 2.00 A), not the geometry that produced legacy/FePorph_1_Window.dat, which is not in this repository. So it will NOT reproduce the legacy energy of -2201.53 Ha, and it is not supposed to. What it does test is the pipeline on an open-shell-capable transition metal at the scale the method was built for. Expect NFC=82, NFV=NBsUse-103, NELEC=22, MS2=0.

